IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`
IMPORT `sca-p2-constitution`

-- Tests for Part 2 (ss 3 to 8).  Every expected value is written from the text beside the assertion, never from the code's output.

-- s 3(1): five State Courts are named; the list is not closed, so any other body is not decided.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the court is one of the State Courts` `District Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the court is one of the State Courts` `Magistrate's Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the court is one of the State Courts` `Coroner's Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the court is one of the State Courts` `Small Claims Tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the court is one of the State Courts` `Employment Claims Tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the court is one of the State Courts` `General Division of the High Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the court is one of the State Courts` `Another court or tribunal` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 3(1A), (2), (4), (5): each names the court it is about and nothing else.
#ASSERT `s 3(1A) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by this Act and any other written law` `District Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1A) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by this Act and any other written law` `Magistrate's Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1A) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by this Act and any other written law` `Coroner's Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984 and any other written law` `Small Claims Tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984 and any other written law` `District Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by the Coroners Act 2010 and any other written law` `Coroner's Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by the Coroners Act 2010 and any other written law` `Magistrate's Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by the Employment Claims Act 2016 and any other written law` `Employment Claims Tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by the Employment Claims Act 2016 and any other written law` `Small Claims Tribunal` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ss 4 and 5.
#ASSERT `s 4 the State Court is constituted by the President under an appropriate name` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 the State Court is constituted by the President under an appropriate name` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5 the State Courts have and use a seal of the nature the Chief Justice has prescribed as the section requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5 the State Courts have and use a seal of the nature the Chief Justice has prescribed as the section requires` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 6: signed and sealed (and no Rules of Court otherwise) -> yes; a bare "must" not met -> not decided; "Subject to Rules of Court" -> not decided.
#ASSERT `s 6 the process of the State Courts is signed by a judicial officer and bears the seal of the court as the section requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 the process of the State Courts is signed by a judicial officer and bears the seal of the court as the section requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6 the process of the State Courts is signed by a judicial officer and bears the seal of the court as the section requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6 the process of the State Courts is signed by a judicial officer and bears the seal of the court as the section requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 6A(1): sits every day except Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays.
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) the State Court is to sit on the day` `Ordinary day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) the State Court is to sit on the day` Saturday EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) the State Court is to sit on the day` Sunday EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) the State Court is to sit on the day` `Public holiday` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) the State Court is to sit on the day` `Day in a vacation authorised under section 61` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 6A(2): a judicial officer may sit on those days if directed, or if the business is extremely urgent in the officer's opinion.
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the judicial officer may lawfully sit on the day` `Ordinary day` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the judicial officer may lawfully sit on the day` Saturday TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the judicial officer may lawfully sit on the day` Saturday FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the judicial officer may lawfully sit on the day` Saturday FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the judicial officer may lawfully sit on the day` Sunday FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the judicial officer may lawfully sit on the day` `Public holiday` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the judicial officer may lawfully sit on the day` `Day in a vacation authorised under section 61` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the judicial officer may lawfully sit on the day` `Day in a vacation authorised under section 61` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 6A(3) the State Court sits at the time and place the Chief Justice has appointed as the section requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(3) the State Court sits at the time and place the Chief Justice has appointed as the section requires` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 7(1), (2), (2AA), (2AB).
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the place is deemed an open and public court to which the public may have access` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the place is deemed an open and public court to which the public may have access` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the State Court has power to hear the matter or part of it in private` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the State Court has power to hear the matter or part of it in private` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(2AA) the application is to be heard in private` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2AA) the application is to be heard in private` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2AB) the State Court has power to hear the subsection (2AA) application otherwise than in private` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2AB) the State Court has power to hear the subsection (2AA) application otherwise than in private` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(2AB) the State Court has power to hear the subsection (2AA) application otherwise than in private` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 7(2A): three kinds of material; satisfied -> may order; not satisfied -> may not; other material -> not decided.
#ASSERT `s 7(2A) the State Court may order the material to be removed or sufficiently redacted` `The name, address or photograph of a witness` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2A) the State Court may order the material to be removed or sufficiently redacted` `The name, address or photograph of a witness` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(2A) the State Court may order the material to be removed or sufficiently redacted` `Evidence or another thing likely to lead to the identification of a witness by a person other than a party` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2A) the State Court may order the material to be removed or sufficiently redacted` `Information that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2A) the State Court may order the material to be removed or sufficiently redacted` `Other material` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 7(3): three kinds of act an order may forbid.
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the State Court may at any time order that no person is to do the act` `Publish the name, address or photograph of a witness, or evidence likely to lead to the identification of a witness` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the State Court may at any time order that no person is to do the act` `Do another act likely to lead to the identification of a witness` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the State Court may at any time order that no person is to do the act` `Publish information that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the State Court may at any time order that no person is to do the act` `Another act` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 7(4): the offence, and the greatest punishment: a fine of $5,000, imprisonment of 12 months, or both.
#ASSERT `s 7(4) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(4) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(4) the punishment is within the greatest the offence allows` 5_000 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(4) the punishment is within the greatest the offence allows` 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(4) the punishment is within the greatest the offence allows` 5_001 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(4) the punishment is within the greatest the offence allows` 0 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 7(5): a private hearing; the court permits (in its discretion) a journalist, an interested individual or another individual it specifies.
#ASSERT `s 7(5) the individual may be present in the courtroom while the matter is heard in private` FALSE `A journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(5) the individual may be present in the courtroom while the matter is heard in private` TRUE `A journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(5) the individual may be present in the courtroom while the matter is heard in private` TRUE `A journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(5) the individual may be present in the courtroom while the matter is heard in private` TRUE `An individual whom the court determines has a sufficient interest in the matter or proceeding` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(5) the individual may be present in the courtroom while the matter is heard in private` TRUE `Another individual that the court specifies in the particular case` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(5) the individual may be present in the courtroom while the matter is heard in private` TRUE `Anyone else` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 7(6) and (7).
#ASSERT `s 7(6) the matter is one the State Court may consider in deciding whether to hear the matter in private` `Whether the defence of an accused person will be prejudiced by the presence of a member of the public` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(6) the matter is one the State Court may consider in deciding whether to hear the matter in private` `Whether an accused person or witness has a legitimate interest in privacy that needs to be protected` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(6) the matter is one the State Court may consider in deciding whether to hear the matter in private` `Whether the object of the matter will be defeated by publicity if heard in open court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(6) the matter is one the State Court may consider in deciding whether to hear the matter in private` `Whether an accused person or witness has a legitimate interest in protecting the confidentiality of information that may be disclosed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(6) the matter is one the State Court may consider in deciding whether to hear the matter in private` `Whether information that may be disclosed will be prejudicial to the interests of Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(6) the matter is one the State Court may consider in deciding whether to hear the matter in private` `Another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(7) "broadcasting service" the service is a broadcasting service` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(7) "broadcasting service" the service is a broadcasting service` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(7) "newspaper" the publication is a newspaper` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(7) "newspaper" the publication is a newspaper` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 8(1): any matter (other than one prescribed) through a live video, television or audio link, or other electronic means the Chief Justice approves.
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the State Court may conduct the hearing through the means` FALSE `A live video link` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the State Court may conduct the hearing through the means` FALSE `A live television link` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the State Court may conduct the hearing through the means` FALSE `A live audio link` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the State Court may conduct the hearing through the means` FALSE `Another electronic means of communication approved by the Chief Justice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the State Court may conduct the hearing through the means` FALSE `Another electronic means of communication not approved by the Chief Justice` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the State Court may conduct the hearing through the means` TRUE `A live video link` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 8(2): subsection (1) does not affect three provisions of other Acts.
#ASSERT `s 8(2) subsection (1) affects the operation of the provision` `Section 26A of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(2) subsection (1) affects the operation of the provision` `Section 62A of the Evidence Act 1893` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(2) subsection (1) affects the operation of the provision` `Section 281 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(2) subsection (1) affects the operation of the provision` `Another provision` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 8(3): arguments are (criminal oral evidence, civil oral evidence, all parties consent, matter prescribed).
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the State Court may conduct the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the State Court may conduct the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the State Court may conduct the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the State Court may conduct the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the State Court may conduct the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the State Court may conduct the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the bar on a live audio link only applies to the part of the hearing` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the bar on a live audio link only applies to the part of the hearing` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the bar on a live audio link only applies to the part of the hearing` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the bar on a live audio link only applies to the part of the hearing` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the bar on a live audio link only applies to the part of the hearing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 8(4): a temporary, insignificant disruption that did not affect fairness is not audio-only.
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the court is considered to have conducted the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the court is considered to have conducted the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the court is considered to have conducted the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the court is considered to have conducted the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 8(5) the State Court may conduct the hearing in the manner provided under subsection (1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(5) the State Court may conduct the hearing in the manner provided under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the court is deemed to be sitting at a place appointed under section 6A(3)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the court is deemed to be sitting at a place appointed under section 6A(3)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rules, run with #TRACE (a DEONTIC value cannot be compared in #ASSERT on this binary; the traces are read, and the same duties are asserted above as decision functions).
-- s 6: the judicial officer signs and seals: fulfilled.
#TRACE `s 6 duty: a judicial officer must sign the process and the process must bear the seal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A judicial officer` DOES `sign the process and bear the seal of the court` AT 3
-- s 7(4): a person who contravenes an order breaches the prohibition.
#TRACE `s 7(4) duty: any person shall not contravene an order under section 7(2A) or 7(3)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Any person` DOES `contravene an order under section 7(2A) or 7(3)` AT 5
-- s 8(3): a State Court that conducts audio-only breaches the prohibition.
#TRACE `s 8(3) duty: a State Court shall not conduct a part of a hearing through a live audio link only` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A State Court` DOES `conduct a part of a hearing through a live audio link only` AT 2
